<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tivaradeva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tivaradeva was a king of the Panduvamshi dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dakshina-kosala">Dakshina Kosala</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, who reigned in the late 6th century. Known from his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grants, he united the region, styled himself lord of all Kosala and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirpur-chhattisgarh">Shripura</a>, modern Sirpur, his capital. His successors ruled from there until the dynasty declined in the 8th century.</p></div>
